<title>USA: Excel's Ottumwa, Iowa, pork plant to reopen Mar 17.</title>
<headline>Excel's Ottumwa, Iowa, pork plant to reopen Mar 17.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1997-02-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Excel Corp's fire-damaged Ottumwa, Iowa, hog and pork plant will resume full slaughter operations on March 17, said Mark Klein, a company spokesman.</p>
<p>Klein said the plant's other fabrication and boning operations would restart the next day.</p>
<p>&quot;These dates are, of course, predicated on the cooperation of the weather,&quot; Klein said.</p>
<p>The Ottumwa plant, which has the capacity to slaughter 9,600 hogs each day, was damaged by an explosion and fire on January 26. The plant has been closed since the fire.</p>
<p>Excel is a division of  Cargill Inc.</p>
<p>((Chicago newsdesk 312-408-8720))</p>
</text>
